 "rule": "(A24 \"Stub-dependent units\"):\n  1. A step is tagged when, inside it, a rule of the families R-RCV-*, R-MDT-*, R-BR-*, R-DUPKEY, R-XCTL-* or\n     R-COND-ABEND fires, except\n       - the rules that fire on every RECEIVE MAP or every XCTL of the slice whatever the input: R-RCV-NULLFILL,\n         R-MDT-FSET, R-MDT-TYPED, R-XCTL-AID (tagging on them would tag every step after the first);\n       - a field-level rule on a RECEIVE line for a protected field (output only; the program does not read it as\n         input). Protection is read from maps/*.tbl.\n     Every screen unit of a tagged step is tagged.\n  2. A message unit (ERRMSG or INFOMSG) whose legacy text carries a CICS RESP or RESP2 value (RESP, Resp:, Reas:)\n     is tagged, in any step.\n  3. File units: a legacy record that the session changed (it differs from the case's base state, or is new) is\n     tagged when any step that ran WRITE or REWRITE is tagged.",
